<title>USA: Perini Corp Q1 net rises, EPS falls.</title>
<headline>Perini Corp Q1 net rises, EPS falls.</headline>
<dateline>FRAMINGHAM, Mass. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands of Dollars)</p>
<p>							  For the Three</p>
<p>						   Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Revenue from Operations		   $ 327,219   $ 270, 029</p>
<p> Income before Income Taxes		    1,976	  1,602</p>
<p> Provision for Income Taxes		    (115)	  (115)</p>
<p> Net Income					  1,861	  1,487</p>
<p> Earnings per Common Share Outstanding	0.15	   0.20</p>
<p> Average Common Shares Outstanding     4,898,648    4,722,672</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said 1997 Q1 EPS reflects dividends paid to holders of its new Series B cumulative preferred stock, which were not paid in 1996 Q1.</p>
<p>The company said its low tax rate in both periods reflects the realization of tax benefits not recognized in prior years due to accounting limitations.</p>
</text>
